.TH stralloc_erase 3
.SH NAME
stralloc_erase \- clear a stralloc structure
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <stralloc.h>

size_t \fBstralloc_erase\fP(stralloc* \fIsa\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBstralloc_erase\fP clears the contents of the \fIstralloc\fP structure pointed
to by \fIsa\fP. It resets the length to 0 and overwrites the first byte of
the buffer with a 'Z' for diagnostic purposes (offensive programming),
ensuring that any stale data is marked.

It attempts to ensure that the \fIstralloc\fP buffer remains allocated and ready 
for reuse by calling \fBstralloc_ready\fP(3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 if the operation succeeded, 0 if it failed (e.g. out of memory during
internal preparation).
.SH SEE ALSO
stralloc_free(3), stralloc_init(3), stralloc_zero(3), stralloc_ready(3)